tasks.brief:
Constraints: UI_PAGE is one inline HTML string; no external asset references (no http/https src or href); no print/logging; button id is exactly `stopvortex`.

File: src/vortex/ui.py (existing — edit only the named regions).

1. In the `<header>` element, after the existing `<span class="sub">model menu</span>`, add:
   <button id="stopvortex" title="Stop Vortex" style="margin-left:auto">✕ Stop Vortex</button>

2. In the page's `<script>`, next to the other `addEventListener` handlers, add:
   document.getElementById("stopvortex").addEventListener("click", function () {
     if (!confirm("Stop Vortex? This unloads all loaded models, freeing their RAM, and shuts down the server.")) return;
     fetch("/api/shutdown", { method: "POST" })
       .then(function (r) {
         if (!r.ok) throw new Error("shutdown " + r.status);
         document.getElementById("down").style.display = "block";
       })
       .catch(function (e) { setError("Shutdown failed: " + e.message); });
   });

The confirm() message contains the words "unloads" and "models".

Acceptance: the string `id="stopvortex"` appears inside the `<header>...</header>` block; the `confirm(` call and the `/api/shutdown` POST are both present; and the page adds no http/https asset URL.
